A. Core Identity & Objectives
Project: Audio Library Deduplication & Management Tool

Objective: Process, deduplicate, and organize an archive of 50,000+ audio files. The system must utilize acoustic fingerprinting and audio quality metrics to determine the optimal file versions to keep.

Performance Goal: Maximum execution speed and minimum processing delay via efficient multithreading.

Tech Stack: Python 3.x, SQLite, Mutagen, AcoustID.

B. Architecture & Module Map
(Note: Update these filenames to match your actual local structure)

main.py: Application entry point; orchestrates the multithreaded detection script and manages the thread pool.

fingerprint.py: Handles audio fingerprint generation and API calls via AcoustID.

metadata.py: Reads, parses, and updates audio file tags using Mutagen.

database.py: Manages the SQLite connection, schema initialization, and CRUD operations.

dedupe_logic.py: Contains the core logic for evaluating quality metrics and fingerprint matches to isolate duplicates.

C. Immutable Constraints & Rules
Rule 1: Thread Safety: All SQLite database writes must be strictly thread-safe. Use a robust connection pooling method or a dedicated queue to prevent locking errors during high-speed concurrent processing.

Rule 2: Safe Deletion: Do not implement automatic, permanent deletion of duplicate files. Duplicates must be flagged in the database or moved to a quarantine directory for final review.

Rule 3: AI Code Modifications: When assisting with this project, generate or modify only the specific function, class, or method requested. Never output a full file rewrite unless explicitly commanded.

Rule 4: Documentation: All new functions must include standard Python type hints and concise docstrings.

